  "name": "Altiverruca Beringiana sp. n. (Crustacea, Cirripedia): First Record of Verrucomorphan Barnacle in the North Pacific",
  "description": "In bottom samples gathered in the vicinity of Bering Island by R/V Mstislav Keldysh during its 22nd voyage, several specimens of Verrucomorpha were found belonging to a new species Altiverruca beringiana sp. n. The new species resembles A. sculpturata Zevina. Before this find, the verrucomorph cirripeds were never known about the 30 degree N latitude in the boreal Pacific. Taking into account earlier data, it can be assumed that the distribution area of this suborder of Cirripedia includes the entire World Ocean.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: A report on the Altiverruca beringiana sp. n. (Crustacea, Cirripedia): First record of verrucomorphan barnacle in the North Pacific",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23564571",
